  "body": "### What is the issue with the HTML Standard?\n\nCurrently when I look up the `width` or `height` attributes anywhere in the spec it shows a description that is the same text over and over again. [Example from the img element’s width](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/embedded-content.html#the-img-element:attr-dim-width):\r\n\r\n> [width](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/embedded-content-other.html#attr-dim-width) — Horizontal dimension; Horizontal dimension; Horizontal dimension; Horizontal dimension; Horizontal dimension; Horizontal dimension; Horizontal dimension\r\n\r\nI could not find this repetition in the source file, so I am not a 100% sure where this would need to be fixed. It reads very much like a bug, even if it technically might not be.",
